1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,884
Mempire is a real-time card battler for

2
00:00:02,904 --> 00:00:05,496
crypto-native players who want real stakes,

3
00:00:05,516 --> 00:00:07,250
without seed phrases, faucets,

4
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:08,750
or wallet popups.

5
00:00:09,313 --> 00:00:12,010
Every coin, memecoin and stock is a

6
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:14,378
fighter, and the market decides who is

7
00:00:14,398 --> 00:00:15,472
strong today.

8
00:00:15,664 --> 00:00:17,327
Everything you see is live,

9
00:00:17,347 --> 00:00:19,130
on Monad testnet.

10
00:00:19,730 --> 00:00:22,067
Signing up takes one passkey prompt,

11
00:00:22,087 --> 00:00:23,266
through Mera.

12
00:00:23,457 --> 00:00:25,039
The account key is derived from the

13
00:00:25,059 --> 00:00:27,953
passkey's PRF output, so there is no

14
00:00:27,973 --> 00:00:29,323
seed phrase to lose,

15
00:00:29,343 --> 00:00:31,332
and the same passkey brings the same

16
00:00:31,352 --> 00:00:33,494
account back on any device.

17
00:00:34,094 --> 00:00:37,467
The heartbeat subscribes to Monad's new-heads stream.

18
00:00:37,821 --> 00:00:39,566
Each block moves from proposed,

19
00:00:39,586 --> 00:00:42,262
to voted in about three hundred milliseconds,

20
00:00:42,291 --> 00:00:44,279
to finalized in under six hundred,

21
00:00:44,299 --> 00:00:46,186
timed right here in the browser.

22
00:00:46,186 --> 00:00:48,662
On first sign-in, our relayer mints an

23
00:00:48,682 --> 00:00:52,322
eight-card starter deck as ERC-721s,

24
00:00:52,351 --> 00:00:55,349
requests test AUSD from Agora's faucet,

25
00:00:55,369 --> 00:00:57,370
and drips a little MON for gas,

26
00:00:57,390 --> 00:01:00,693
while keeping Monad's ten-MON reserve balance.

27
00:01:01,293 --> 00:01:03,781
The Cards screen shows every fighter's live

28
00:01:03,801 --> 00:01:06,056
price, its twenty-four-hour move,

29
00:01:06,076 --> 00:01:07,789
and the on-chain meta.

30
00:01:08,236 --> 00:01:10,468
Minting pulls a signed Pyth price update

31
00:01:10,488 --> 00:01:12,456
into the mint transaction itself,

32
00:01:12,531 --> 00:01:14,009
and the card records the price it

33
00:01:14,029 --> 00:01:15,243
was minted at.

34
00:01:15,843 --> 00:01:16,926
Back in the arena,

35
00:01:16,946 --> 00:01:19,251
the side boards are the market meta.

36
00:01:19,512 --> 00:01:22,325
A Chainlink CRE workflow reads prices,

37
00:01:22,345 --> 00:01:25,157
reaches consensus, and writes bounded buffs and

38
00:01:25,177 --> 00:01:27,227
nerfs to the MarketMeta contract.

39
00:01:27,581 --> 00:01:29,534
Each match locks the epoch it starts

40
00:01:29,554 --> 00:01:30,304
on.

41
00:01:30,304 --> 00:01:31,909
We stake the one-dollar tier,

42
00:01:31,929 --> 00:01:32,899
in MON.

43
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,847
The stake, the deck lock,

44
00:01:34,867 --> 00:01:36,902
and a per-match session key are funded

45
00:01:36,922 --> 00:01:39,305
in one transaction, and the second player

46
00:01:39,325 --> 00:01:41,421
joins the same match on chain.

47
00:01:42,021 --> 00:01:43,882
During the match, every card I drop

48
00:01:43,902 --> 00:01:45,670
is its own Monad transaction,

49
00:01:45,690 --> 00:01:47,330
signed by the session key,

50
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:48,900
so there are no popups.

51
00:01:49,161 --> 00:01:51,452
Each pill shows the real round trip:

52
00:01:51,472 --> 00:01:53,254
executed, then final.

53
00:01:53,701 --> 00:01:56,807
Both seats also post state-hash checkpoints.

54
00:01:57,521 --> 00:01:59,594
We fast-forward the middle of the match.

55
00:01:59,727 --> 00:02:02,229
A tower falls, in slow motion.

56
00:02:31,083 --> 00:02:33,411
When the second player's claim lands,

57
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:35,335
the contract settles the pot in that

58
00:02:35,355 --> 00:02:36,720
same transaction:

59
00:02:36,911 --> 00:02:38,415
ninety percent to the winner,

60
00:02:38,444 --> 00:02:40,444
ten percent rake, and a chest for

61
00:02:40,464 --> 00:02:41,410
the winner.

62
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:48,807
Clans are the social layer.

63
00:02:49,069 --> 00:02:51,044
These clans were seeded by our team

64
00:02:51,064 --> 00:02:52,104
for the demo.

65
00:02:52,458 --> 00:02:54,481
Joining one puts us straight into its

66
00:02:54,501 --> 00:02:57,070
clan war, a bracket scored only by

67
00:02:57,090 --> 00:02:59,462
staked wins the relay has verified on

68
00:02:59,482 --> 00:03:00,393
chain.

69
00:03:02,583 --> 00:03:04,180
Empire is your record.

70
00:03:04,371 --> 00:03:07,941
It reads Monad's staking precompile live,

71
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:11,120
through Multicall3, and it verifies a passkey

72
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:15,009
signature on chain with Monad's P-256 precompile,

73
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:16,460
for a fraction of the gas a

74
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,530
Solidity verifier needs.

75
00:03:20,583 --> 00:03:22,966
The leaderboards rank trophies,

76
00:03:22,986 --> 00:03:25,416
and money columns that the relay credits

77
00:03:25,436 --> 00:03:27,715
only after it verifies each settlement on

78
00:03:27,735 --> 00:03:28,635
chain.

79
00:03:29,235 --> 00:03:32,617
Finally, the proof page reads transactions live

80
00:03:32,637 --> 00:03:33,734
from the chain:

81
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:36,405
the Chainlink report that wrote the meta,

82
00:03:36,433 --> 00:03:38,654
a mint with its Pyth price update,

83
00:03:38,674 --> 00:03:40,305
and a gasless chest,

84
00:03:40,334 --> 00:03:45,809
a type-four transaction with an EIP-7702 authorization,

85
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,430
run through the canonical EntryPoint and paid

86
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:50,476
for by our own paymaster.

87
00:03:51,076 --> 00:03:51,930
Mempire.

88
00:03:52,005 --> 00:03:53,169
Every coin is a fighter.

89
00:03:53,189 --> 00:03:55,050
Play it now, at mempire monad,

90
00:03:55,070 --> 00:03:56,806
dot vercel, dot app.
